We simulate a lost-sales inventory system. There is no stochastic prediction and no missing information beyond the explicit reporting cutoff.

We have:

- Receipts add quantity to stock.
- Demands consume min(stock, quantity); any unmet quantity is lost (never backlogged). 
- A stockout means strictly positive unmet demand, not merely ending with zero stock.

We have raw report histories. We must keep reports with received_time <= knowledge_cutoff (given). Then choose the highest visible revision for each event_id. Revisions replace earlier reports, not add to them. Then keep chosen events with event_time <= target_time. Apply these events in (event_time, event_id) order, starting from initial_stock. Ignore any report not visible at the knowledge cutoff even if its event occurred earlier. Arrival order is not event order.

